# Sir Ottokar the Late (NPC plan batch 5; docs/plans/npc_depth_and_quests.md): a dead knight of the Order who arrived late to its last
# battle and has been late to everything since. He turns up in the grounds after every fight at Argynvostholt and asks if he
# missed it. Wants to be on time once. Secret: he was late because he stopped to help a farmer's wife with her cart, and would
# again. No quest, no check that matters. Lines drafted by Gemini through the ai-bridge, edited; every line here is unvoiced.

~ start
if not flag.ottokar_met
set ottokar_met
Narrator: Pale hooves clatter across the flagstones just as the dust settles. A phantom rider reins in hard, his helm slightly askew.
Sir Ottokar the Late: Hold! Stand fast, my brothers, I am with you! Wait. Did I miss it?
Sir Ottokar the Late [weary]: Pray forgive me. The stairs collapsed three hundred years ago, and my horse still insists on taking the hallway.
Sir Ottokar the Late [smile]: Sir Ottokar of the Silver Dragon, at your service. They call me the Late, and not solely for my condition.
Sir Ottokar the Late: If you intend to be ambushed again in the next room, do give a louder shout.
-> menu
endif
set ottokar_visits += 1
if flag.ottokar_visits == 1
Sir Ottokar the Late: Make way! My lance is levelled and my oath is sworn! Oh, you have already wiped your blades.
Sir Ottokar the Late [weary]: Did I miss it? I swear to you, I started galloping the very moment I heard the first scream.
elif flag.ottokar_visits == 2
Sir Ottokar the Late: The buckle on my greave caught upon the tapestry in the west gallery. Did I miss it?
Sir Ottokar the Late: You dispatch them with remarkable haste. It leaves very little room for a chivalrous rescue.
else
Sir Ottokar the Late: Do not tell me that was the last of them. Did I miss it again?
Sir Ottokar the Late [smile]: At least the dead are still dead when I arrive. One must find comfort where one can.
endif
-> menu

~ menu
* What do you want, Sir Ottokar? -> want
* [if flag.ottokar_wanted and not flag.ottokar_secret_known] [Insight DC 12] (He laughs a beat too quickly.) -> secret_ok | secret_miss
* What does Lord Vladimir think of you? -> about_vladimir
* Farewell, Sir Ottokar. -> END

~ want
set ottokar_wanted
Sir Ottokar the Late: Only to arrive while a sword is still raised in anger, just once before this manor falls to dust.
Sir Ottokar the Late [weary]: I should like to shout our battle cry before the battle is entirely concluded.
Sir Ottokar the Late: Even the third blow would suffice. I am not a greedy man.
-> menu

~ secret_ok
set ottokar_secret_known
Narrator: His easy smile fades. You see it is not the tardiness that weighs on him, but the truth he keeps behind it.
Sir Ottokar the Late [sad]: On the day of the last battle, a farmer's wife had lost a cartwheel in the ditch by the crossroads. The mud was up to the axle.
Sir Ottokar the Late: I could not leave an old woman in the rain with night coming on. When I reached the hill, the banners were already down.
Sir Ottokar the Late: I have never told the others, lest they think I offer an excuse. Yet if the wheel broke tomorrow, I would stop again.
-> menu

~ secret_miss
Sir Ottokar the Late [smile]: Ah, well, my horse was bred for endurance rather than haste, and eternity has not improved her trot.
-> menu

~ about_vladimir
Sir Ottokar the Late [smile]: Lord Vladimir says I am a fine knight and a terrible clock.
Sir Ottokar the Late: He never strikes my name from the roster, though. He merely writes it at the bottom of the page.
-> menu
